		<div class="ps-page-title"> 
			<h1 id="skip">Notice of the right to opt-out of selling or sharing personal information</h1>
		</div>

		
	

		<div data-exo-id="exo-marketing" aria-hidden="true"> </div>
		
		<!-- Body Region -->
		
	
		

	<div class="enhanced-txt-cm text-aligned-left" data-cid="tcm:84-314341-16" data-ctid="tcm:91-223644-32">

		<div>
			
			<div class="enhanced-txt-body">

				<div class="title2-SemiBold"><h2  >Set cookie preferences on our site</h2></div>

				

				<div class="subheadline-regular" ><p>If you don’t want us to share personal information with third parties for advertising purposes, you may manage your preferences below. For more information, see our <a href="/privacy-security/online/">Digital Privacy and Cookies Policy</a>.</p></div>

				

				

				

				

				

				

			</div>
		</div>
	</div>

	
		
	<div class="manage-cookies-btn" > <button id="ot-sdk-btn" class="ot-sdk-show-settings btn ps-btn-secondary">Manage cookies </button> </div>

	
		

	<div class="enhanced-txt-cm text-aligned-left" data-cid="tcm:84-314342-16" data-ctid="tcm:91-223644-32">

		<div>
			
			<div class="enhanced-txt-body">

				<div class="title2-SemiBold"><h2  >Set cookie preferences via your browser</h2></div>

				

				<div class="subheadline-regular" ><p>You can also set your cookie preferences at the browser level through a service called Global Privacy Control (GPC). You enable this service through specific browsers or browser extensions (see which browsers are GPC-enabled at the <a data-exit="true" aria-label="Global Privacy Control opens dialogue"  data-href-id="1314325702" href="#">Global Privacy Control</a> website). Once you activate the GPC setting, your browser will automatically send participating websites (like ours) a “do not sell or share my personal information” signal.</p></div>

				

				

				

				

				

				

			</div>
		</div>
	</div>

	


		
		
	


		
		

		
